{"text": " Kenya loses an estimated 100 billion Kenyan shillings in agricultural produce to post-harvest losses every year. The majority of those losses happen not in the field but between the farm gate and the consumer in storage, transit and handling. AI cannot eliminate post-harvest losses but it can identify where they are highest and prescribe the interventions that save the most value per shilling spent. In this lesson, the post-harvest loss problem in East African supply chains, where losses occur, why and how AI can be used to systematically identify and reduce the most impactful loss points. Covers storage condition optimization, quality grading with AI vision, transit route analysis and the WhatsApp advisory model for small holder storage decisions. We cover the post-harvest loss map, where in the storage condition data, temperature, humidity and grain moisture content as predictors of spoilage. AI assisted quality grading using image analysis to grade produce at point of collection and transit time analysis, how route and vehicle quality correlates with produce damage in East African logistics. Post-harvest losses in East Africa occur at four main stages with different AI applications at each stage. One, on farm storage, this is where the largest losses occur for small holders. Grain stored at above 14% moisture content develops aflatoxin mould within six to eight weeks. The most valuable post-harvest AI systems in East Africa are not the ones with the most sophisticated AI. They are the ones that reach the most farmers with the most actionable recommendations delivered through the channels farmers already use. A WhatsApp message with a cell slash store recommendation based on a moisture reading and a weather forecast changes a farmer's behaviour. A complex AI dashboard that requires internet access and a smartphone does not. Remember this, map where the losses actually happen before building any AI solution. The most sophisticated storage AI system is worthless if the highest losses occur in transit. Always start with data on where value is being lost, not with the technology you want to use. Apply what you learn in this lesson and you will see results immediately. Your skills bear fruit.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 7.38, "text": " Kenya loses an estimated 100 billion Kenyan shillings in agricultural produce", "tokens": [50364, 31011, 18293, 364, 14109, 2319, 5218, 8273, 6277, 402, 373, 1109, 294, 19587, 5258, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1652019953323623, "compression_ratio": 1.4636871508379887, "no_speech_prob": 0.009998267516493797, "words": [{"word": " Kenya", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.42, "probability": 0.9398530125617981}, {"word": " loses", "start": 0.42, "end": 0.98, "probability": 0.9849763512611389}, {"word": " an", "start": 0.98, "end": 1.38, "probability": 0.9535385966300964}, {"word": " estimated", "start": 1.38, "end": 2.08, "probability": 0.9995993971824646}, {"word": " 100", "start": 2.08, "end": 3.36, "probability": 0.8474664688110352}, {"word": " billion", "start": 3.36, "end": 3.98, "probability": 0.9687619805335999}, {"word": " Kenyan", "start": 3.98, "end": 4.6, "probability": 0.740770548582077}, {"word": " shillings", "start": 4.6, "end": 5.3, "probability": 0.9074634114901224}, {"word": " in", "start": 5.3, "end": 5.8, "probability": 0.9873944520950317}, {"word": " agricultural", "start": 5.8, "end": 6.4, "probability": 0.9782796502113342}, {"word": " produce", "start": 6.4, "end": 7.38, "probability": 0.9892115592956543}]}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 7.38, "end": 14.92, "text": " to post-harvest losses every year. The majority of those losses happen not in the field", "tokens": [50748, 281, 2183, 12, 5854, 5571, 15352, 633, 1064, 13, 440, 6286, 295, 729, 15352, 1051, 406, 294, 264, 2519, 51124], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1652019953323623, "compression_ratio": 1.4636871508379887, "no_speech_prob": 0.009998267516493797, "words": [{"word